      "query": "What is the latest runbook for the payment-service incident?",
      "answer": "Based on 8 relevant items from Confluence, Jira, Slack, Google Drive:\n\n**Payment Service Incident Runbook** [Confluence]: Payment-service runbook. NEW FAILVER STEP: Failover to backup gateway at pg-failover.company.internal if primary is down for more than 5 minutes. Updated at 1:00 PM today. (last updated: 10/6/2026, 4:56:51 PM)\n\n**Set up monitoring for new payment gateway** [Jira] (Done, P2, assigned to Mike Rodriguez): We're switching to Stripe. Set up Datadog monitors for: payment success rate, webhook latency, refund volume. Create a dashboard for the finance team. Alert on error rate > 1%.\n\n**##engineering** [Slack] — Jennifer Park said: \"Payment service is having intermittent errors! Error rate jumped to 3%. Investigating now. If anyone has the latest runbook, please share it.\"\n\n**Deployment Runbook** [Confluence]: To deploy: 1) Run tests. 2) Create PR to main. 3) CI runs automatically. 4) Monitor dashboards. 5) If errors, rollback with ./rollback.sh. Always post in #engineering before deploying! (last updated: 10/4/2026, 2:00:00 PM)\n\n**Refactor authentication middleware** [Jira] (To Do, P2, assigned to Jennifer Park): Current auth middleware is 500 lines of nested callbacks. Refactor to async/await, add unit tests (target 80% coverage), and extract JWT validation into its own module. No behavior changes.\n\n**Implement pagination for search results** [Jira] (To Do, P2, assigned to Sarah Chen): Search currently returns all results at once. For large queries this causes timeouts. Implement cursor-based pagination, 20 results per page. Add metadata for total count and next cursor.\n\n**Onboarding Checklist for New Hires.pdf** [Google Drive]: Day 1: laptop setup, email, Slack, VPN. Week 1: meet team, codebase access, dev environment setup. Week 2: first small task assigned. 30 days: check-in with manager. 60 days: first PR merged. 90 days: performance review.\n\n**VPN Setup Instructions** [Confluence]: Download the VPN client from the IT portal. Use your SSO credentials. Connect to vpn.company.internal. If you get certificate errors, contact IT support. VPN is required for accessing internal systems remotely.",
