      "query": "Show me the security incident report from the Q3 breach",
      "answer": "Based on 8 relevant items from Confluence, Google Drive, Slack:\n\n**VPN Setup Instructions** [Confluence]: Download the VPN client from the IT portal. Use your SSO credentials. Connect to vpn.company.internal. If you get certificate errors, contact IT support. VPN is required for accessing internal systems remotely.\n\n**Team Building Event Photos.zip** [Google Drive]: Photos from the September team building event: escape room, dinner, karaoke. Great turnout - 85% of the office participated. Next event: October Halloween costume contest and pumpkin carving.\n\n**Company Onboarding Guide** [Confluence]: Welcome to the company! This guide covers your first week: setting up your laptop, accessing email, joining Slack channels, and meeting your team. HR will schedule orientation on day one.\n\n**Brand Guidelines** [Confluence]: Logo colors: primary #1A73E8, secondary #FF6D00. Font: Inter for all materials. Logo must have minimum clear space equal to the height of the 'o' in the logo. Never stretch or recolor the logo.\n\n**Customer Service FAQ** [Confluence]: Common customer questions: Q: How do I reset my password? A: Click 'Forgot Password' on the login page. Q: How do I upgrade my plan? A: Go to Settings > Billing > Upgrade. Q: How do I contact support? A: Email support@company.com or use the in-app chat. These are public-facing answers for customer service representatives.\n\n**##random** [Slack] — Mike Rodriguez said: \"Someone left a cake in the kitchen. It says 'Sorry for the 502s'. I think the staging server is apologizing.\"\n\n**##general** [Slack] — HR Bot said: \"Open enrollment starts October 15! Review your benefits at benefits.company.internal. Changes must be submitted by October 31. Questions? Come to the HR office hours on Wednesday.\"\n\n**##general** [Slack] — CEO Rachel said: \"Great work everyone on closing Q3! We hit 112% of our revenue target. The Acme Corp deal was a game-changer. Let's keep the momentum going in Q4. Details Friday at all-hands.\"",
